    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n57807" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κλέπτ-ης</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ου</span>, ὁ, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>thief</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Il.
				3.11
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὸν πυρὸς κ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.
					<u>Pr.</u>
					946
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κλέπτα δύο</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Ar.
					<u>V.</u>
					928
				</span></i>
			; opp. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἅρπαξ</span> (a robber),
				<i><span class="en">
				Myrtil.
				4
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λῃστὰς ἢ κλέπτας</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pl.
					<u>R.</u>
					351c
				</span></i>
			, cf.<i><span class="en">
				<u>Ev.Jo.</u>
				10.8
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὁ τοῦ κ. λόγος</span>, a
			logical fallacy, <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>SE</u>
				180b18
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> generally,
				<i>cheat, knave</i>, <i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>Aj.</u>
				1135
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κακῶν ἀλλοτρίων κ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					D.
					45.59
				</span></i>
			.</div>
